---
permalink: /sitemap.xml
layout: null
sitemap: false
---
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
{%- comment -%}
Generated from the collections. A page leaves the sitemap by setting
`sitemap: false` in its front matter (used for the noindex alias page).
<lastmod> comes from the last commit that touched the source file
(_plugins/lastmod.rb), so it cannot drift the way the hand-maintained
`sitemap_lastmod` front matter did. Set that key only to override deliberately.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign pages = site.pages | where_exp: "p", "p.sitemap != false" | where_exp: "p", "p.title" -%}
{%- assign docs = site.documents | where_exp: "d", "d.sitemap != false" -%}
{%- assign all = pages | concat: docs -%}
{%- assign sorted = all | sort: "priority" | reverse -%}
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9
        http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9/sitemap.xsd">
{% for p in sorted %}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ p.url | absolute_url }}</loc>
    {%- comment -%}
    `p.date` is deliberately NOT a blanket fallback. Jekyll gives a collection
    document with no `date:` in its front matter the *build* time, so using it
    stamped ten URLs with the date of the last deploy -- a modification date
    that changes every rebuild and reflects nothing. An absent <lastmod> is a
    weaker signal than a real one, but a fabricated one is worse than both: it
    trains Google to discount the field. So `p.date` counts only when it is a
    real publish date, i.e. not today's build.

    This is a guard, not the fix. The fix is `_plugins/lastmod.rb` supplying
    `git_lastmod` for every page, which requires Settings -> Pages -> Source to
    be "GitHub Actions"; the legacy branch build runs Jekyll in safe mode and
    skips _plugins entirely.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign lastmod = p.sitemap_lastmod | default: p.last_modified | default: p.git_lastmod %}
    {%- unless lastmod %}
      {%- assign page_day = p.date | date: "%Y-%m-%d" %}
      {%- assign build_day = site.time | date: "%Y-%m-%d" %}
      {%- if p.date and page_day != build_day %}{% assign lastmod = p.date %}{% endif %}
    {%- endunless %}
    {%- if lastmod %}
    <lastmod>{{ lastmod | date: "%Y-%m-%d" }}</lastmod>
    {%- endif %}
    <changefreq>{{ p.changefreq | default: "monthly" }}</changefreq>
    <priority>{{ p.priority | default: 0.5 }}</priority>
  </url>
{% endfor %}
</urlset>
